    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Problem: Variational Dropout in RNNs for Language Modeling\n",
        "\n",
        "## Problem Statement\n",
        "You are tasked with implementing **Variational Dropout** (also known as locked dropout) for an LSTM network on a language modeling task. Unlike naive dropout which samples a new dropout mask at each timestep, variational dropout uses the **same dropout mask across all timesteps** in a sequence, which has been shown to improve regularization in RNNs.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objectives\n",
        "1. Implement a custom LSTM with **Variational Dropout** (locked dropout across time steps)\n",
        "2. Implement a baseline LSTM with **Naive Dropout** (standard dropout at each timestep)\n",
        "3. Train both models on a language modeling dataset (Penn Treebank)\n",
        "4. Compare the performance and training stability of both approaches\n",
        "5. Visualize training curves to demonstrate the difference\n",
        "\n",
        "### Requirements\n",
        "- Implement `VariationalDropout` layer that maintains the same mask across timesteps\n",
        "- Create two LSTM models: one with variational dropout, one with naive dropout\n",
        "- Use perplexity as the evaluation metric\n",
        "- Visualize and compare training/validation loss curves\n",
        "\n",
        "### Dataset\n",
        "**Penn Treebank (PTB)**: A standard benchmark for language modeling containing Wall Street Journal articles.\n",
        "\n",
        "<details>\n",
        "  <summary>💡 Hint</summary>\n",
        "  \n",
        "  **Variational Dropout**: Sample the dropout mask once per sequence and apply it at every timestep. This can be implemented by generating a mask of shape `(batch_size, hidden_size)` and reusing it.\n",
        "  \n",
        "  **Naive Dropout**: Use standard PyTorch dropout which samples a new mask at each forward pass.\n",
        "  \n",
        "  **Key Difference**: Variational dropout prevents the network from learning to rely on specific timestep patterns, leading to better generalization.\n",
        "</details>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 1: Import Libraries and Setup"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import torch\n",
        "import torch.nn as nn\n",
        "import torch.optim as optim\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n",
        "import urllib.request\n",
        "import os\n",
        "from collections import Counter\n",
        "import math\n",
        "\n",
        "# Set random seeds for reproducibility\n",
        "torch.manual_seed(42)\n",
        "np.random.seed(42)\n",
        "\n",
        "device = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')\n",
        "print(f\"Using device: {device}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 2: Data Acquisition and Preprocessing\n",
        "\n",
        "Load the Penn Treebank dataset and prepare it for language modeling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 2,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Downloading Penn Treebank dataset...\n",
            "Downloaded train.txt\n",
            "Downloaded valid.txt\n",
            "Downloaded test.txt\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Download Penn Treebank dataset\n",
        "def download_ptb():\n",
        "    base_url = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wojzaremba/lstm/master/data/'\n",
        "    files = ['ptb.train.txt', 'ptb.valid.txt', 'ptb.test.txt']\n",
        "    \n",
        "    os.makedirs('./data', exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    for file in files:\n",
        "        file_path = f'./data/{file}'\n",
        "        if not os.path.exists(file_path):\n",
        "            print(f\"Downloading {file}...\")\n",
        "            urllib.request.urlretrieve(base_url + file, file_path)\n",
        "        print(f\"Downloaded {file.split('.')[1]}.txt\")\n",
        "\n",
        "download_ptb()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Vocabulary size: 10000\n",
            "Training tokens: 929589\n",
            "Validation tokens: 73760\n",
            "Test tokens: 82430\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Create vocabulary and tokenization\n",
        "class Vocabulary:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, max_size=10000):\n",
        "        self.max_size = max_size\n",
        "        self.word2idx = {'<pad>': 0, '<unk>': 1}\n",
        "        self.idx2word = {0: '<pad>', 1: '<unk>'}\n",
        "        self.word_freq = Counter()\n",
        "        \n",
        "    def build_vocab(self, text):\n",
        "        words = text.split()\n",
        "        self.word_freq.update(words)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Keep most common words\n",
        "        most_common = self.word_freq.most_common(self.max_size - 2)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        for idx, (word, _) in enumerate(most_common, start=2):\n",
        "            self.word2idx[word] = idx\n",
        "            self.idx2word[idx] = word\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def encode(self, text):\n",
        "        words = text.split()\n",
        "        return [self.word2idx.get(word, 1) for word in words]  # 1 is <unk>\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def __len__(self):\n",
        "        return len(self.word2idx)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load data\n",
        "def load_data(file_path):\n",
        "    with open(file_path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
        "        text = f.read().replace('\\n', ' <eos> ')\n",
        "    return text\n",
        "\n",
        "train_text = load_data('./data/ptb.train.txt')\n",
        "valid_text = load_data('./data/ptb.valid.txt')\n",
        "test_text = load_data('./data/ptb.test.txt')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Build vocabulary\n",
        "vocab = Vocabulary(max_size=10000)\n",
        "vocab.build_vocab(train_text)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Encode data\n",
        "train_data = torch.LongTensor(vocab.encode(train_text))\n",
        "valid_data = torch.LongTensor(vocab.encode(valid_text))\n",
        "test_data = torch.LongTensor(vocab.encode(test_text))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Vocabulary size: {len(vocab)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Training tokens: {len(train_data)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Validation tokens: {len(valid_data)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Test tokens: {len(test_data)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Prepare data loaders\n",
        "def batchify(data, batch_size):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Divides data into batch_size separate sequences.\"\"\"\n",
        "    nbatch = data.size(0) // batch_size\n",
        "    data = data.narrow(0, 0, nbatch * batch_size)\n",
        "    data = data.view(batch_size, -1).t().contiguous()\n",
        "    return data\n",
        "\n",
        "def get_batch(source, i, seq_len):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Get a batch of sequences.\"\"\"\n",
        "    seq_len = min(seq_len, len(source) - 1 - i)\n",
        "    data = source[i:i+seq_len]\n",
        "    target = source[i+1:i+1+seq_len]\n",
        "    return data, target\n",
        "\n",
        "batch_size = 20\n",
        "seq_len = 35\n",
        "\n",
        "train_data = batchify(train_data, batch_size).to(device)\n",
        "valid_data = batchify(valid_data, batch_size).to(device)\n",
        "test_data = batchify(test_data, batch_size).to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 3: Model Implementation\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3.1: Implement Variational Dropout Layer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class VariationalDropout(nn.Module):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Implements variational dropout (locked dropout).\n",
        "    The same dropout mask is used across all timesteps.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, dropout_rate=0.5):\n",
        "        super(VariationalDropout, self).__init__()\n",
        "        self.dropout_rate = dropout_rate\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Args:\n",
        "            x: Input tensor of shape (seq_len, batch_size, hidden_size)\n",
        "        Returns:\n",
        "            Dropped out tensor with same shape\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        if not self.training or self.dropout_rate == 0:\n",
        "            return x\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Create mask for the batch and hidden dimensions only\n",
        "        # Shape: (1, batch_size, hidden_size)\n",
        "        mask = x.new_ones(1, x.size(1), x.size(2))\n",
        "        mask = torch.bernoulli(mask * (1 - self.dropout_rate))\n",
        "        mask = mask / (1 - self.dropout_rate)  # Inverted dropout\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Expand mask to all timesteps\n",
        "        mask = mask.expand_as(x)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        return x * mask"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 3.2: Implement LSTM with Variational Dropout"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class LSTMVariational(nn.Module):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    LSTM Language Model with Variational Dropout\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, vocab_size, embed_size, hidden_size, num_layers, dropout=0.5):\n",
        "        super(LSTMVariational, self).__init__()\n",
        "        self.hidden_size = hidden_size\n",
        "        self.num_layers = num_layers\n",
        "        \n",
        "        self.embedding = nn.Embedding(vocab_size, embed_size)\n",
        "        self.lstm = nn.LSTM(embed_size, hidden_size, num_layers, batch_first=False)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Variational dropout layers\n",
        "        self.dropout_embed = VariationalDropout(dropout)\n",
        "        self.dropout_lstm = VariationalDropout(dropout)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        self.fc = nn.Linear(hidden_size, vocab_size)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Tie weights\n",
        "        self.fc.weight = self.embedding.weight\n",
        "        \n",
        "        self.init_weights()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def init_weights(self):\n",
        "        init_range = 0.1\n",
        "        self.embedding.weight.data.uniform_(-init_range, init_range)\n",
        "        self.fc.bias.data.zero_()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def forward(self, x, hidden=None):\n",
        "        # x shape: (seq_len, batch_size)\n",
        "        embed = self.embedding(x)\n",
        "        embed = self.dropout_embed(embed)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        output, hidden = self.lstm(embed, hidden)\n",
        "        output = self.dropout_lstm(output)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Reshape for linear layer\n",
        "        output = output.view(-1, self.hidden_size)\n",
        "        decoded = self.fc(output)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        return decoded, hidden\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def init_hidden(self, batch_size):\n",
        "        weight = next(self.parameters())\n",
        "        return (weight.new_zeros(self.num_layers, batch_size, self.hidden_size),\n",
        "                weight.new_zeros(self.num_layers, batch_size, self.hidden_size))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 3.3: Implement LSTM with Naive Dropout"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 7,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class LSTMNaive(nn.Module):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    LSTM Language Model with Naive (Standard) Dropout\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, vocab_size, embed_size, hidden_size, num_layers, dropout=0.5):\n",
        "        super(LSTMNaive, self).__init__()\n",
        "        self.hidden_size = hidden_size\n",
        "        self.num_layers = num_layers\n",
        "        \n",
        "        self.embedding = nn.Embedding(vocab_size, embed_size)\n",
        "        self.lstm = nn.LSTM(embed_size, hidden_size, num_layers, batch_first=False)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Standard dropout layers\n",
        "        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(dropout)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        self.fc = nn.Linear(hidden_size, vocab_size)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Tie weights\n",
        "        self.fc.weight = self.embedding.weight\n",
        "        \n",
        "        self.init_weights()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def init_weights(self):\n",
        "        init_range = 0.1\n",
        "        self.embedding.weight.data.uniform_(-init_range, init_range)\n",
        "        self.fc.bias.data.zero_()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def forward(self, x, hidden=None):\n",
        "        # x shape: (seq_len, batch_size)\n",
        "        embed = self.embedding(x)\n",
        "        embed = self.dropout(embed)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        output, hidden = self.lstm(embed, hidden)\n",
        "        output = self.dropout(output)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Reshape for linear layer\n",
        "        output = output.view(-1, self.hidden_size)\n",
        "        decoded = self.fc(output)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        return decoded, hidden\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def init_hidden(self, batch_size):\n",
        "        weight = next(self.parameters())\n",
        "        return (weight.new_zeros(self.num_layers, batch_size, self.hidden_size),\n",
        "                weight.new_zeros(self.num_layers, batch_size, self.hidden_size))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 4: Training\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4.1: Define Training Function"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 8,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def train_epoch(model, data_source, criterion, optimizer, seq_len, clip=0.25):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Train for one epoch\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    model.train()\n",
        "    total_loss = 0\n",
        "    hidden = model.init_hidden(batch_size)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    for i in range(0, data_source.size(0) - 1, seq_len):\n",
        "        data, targets = get_batch(data_source, i, seq_len)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Detach hidden state\n",
        "        hidden = tuple(h.detach() for h in hidden)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
        "        \n",
        "        output, hidden = model(data, hidden)\n",
        "        loss = criterion(output, targets.view(-1))\n",
        "        \n",
        "        loss.backward()\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Gradient clipping\n",
        "        torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), clip)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        optimizer.step()\n",
        "        \n",
        "        total_loss += loss.item()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    return total_loss / (data_source.size(0) // seq_len)\n",
        "\n",
        "def evaluate(model, data_source, criterion, seq_len):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Evaluate model on validation/test set\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    total_loss = 0\n",
        "    hidden = model.init_hidden(batch_size)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "        for i in range(0, data_source.size(0) - 1, seq_len):\n",
        "            data, targets = get_batch(data_source, i, seq_len)\n",
        "            \n",
        "            output, hidden = model(data, hidden)\n",
        "            loss = criterion(output, targets.view(-1))\n",
        "            \n",
        "            total_loss += loss.item()\n",
        "            \n",
        "            hidden = tuple(h.detach() for h in hidden)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    return total_loss / (data_source.size(0) // seq_len)"
      ]
    },
